; Regression: `*x` on a SCALAR emitted `load i64, i64 %0` -- invalid IR whose
; pointer operand is an integer -- at rc 0 with no diagnostic, and the program
; then died with SIGSEGV wherever that integer happened to point. Nothing ever
; asked: get_pointer_element_type answers null for a non-pointer and the
; prefix arm kept the operand's own type (Planner.report_deref_of_non_pointer#).
; It became urgent with the 2026-08-27 subscript change: `operator []` answers
; the element BY VALUE, so every stale `*a[i]` is exactly this shape.
; Self-hosted-only.
; xfail: cannot dereference a value of type int

function f(n: int) returns int
    *n

print "`f(5)`"
